`/Volumes/Datasec_DEV/!CODING/Datasec/Datasec Security Composer/1_Project_Definition/Briefs/2026-11-10_B1421_STATUS.md`. Sections: STATUS-NOW at the top; BLUF; PRIOR WORK; facts with instrument and control; the premise table (row, cell, runs, reds at main), the diff if any, the red/green comparison under the cap; the CHECKS comparison (main against head, lost 0); moved-main record; UNMEASURED; outside-the-fences disclosure; FOR TUESDAY (which tickets this closes if the gate passes, what you left, whether PR #85 or a Dependabot PR moved). **The LAST line, exactly one of:**
`READY B1421: <sha40>` (the full 40-hex sha of your pushed head; the `git ls-remote` line for your ref prints it), or
`STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY <one question>`.
While running, the last line is `BUILD B1421: <step>`.

## STATUS-NOW (the seat keeps this at the top of STATUS)
Step, lock state (holder text or "mine"), load1, the last command, the next one, the HARD STOP clock.

## Stamp
Tuesday fills each slot at launch; one word or clock each. The unstamped copy reads nine such runs (eight slots and the last line).
